        -:  137:// LIBRARY_TABLE_ROW storage uses std::deque (rather than std::vector) so that pointers and
        -:  138:// references to rows remain valid across push_back/pop_back and erase-at-end operations.
        -:  139:// Code elsewhere (LIB_DATA::row, LIBRARY_MANAGER::m_rowCache) caches raw row pointers that
        -:  140:// must survive runtime mutations from paths like EnsureRemoteLibraryEntry().
        -:  141:typedef std::deque<LIBRARY_TABLE_ROW>::iterator       LIBRARY_TABLE_ROWS_ITER;
        -:  142:typedef std::deque<LIBRARY_TABLE_ROW>::const_iterator LIBRARY_TABLE_ROWS_CITER;
